EXAMPLES=[{'num':'6','title':'Slope Between Two Points','question':'Find the slope through (a) E(2,4), F(4,6); (b) M(3,1), N(−1,3).','steps':['Use m = (y₂−y₁)/(x₂−x₁); both horizontal differences are nonzero.','(a) The vertical difference is 6−4 = 2.','The horizontal difference is 4−2 = 2, so m = 2/2 = 1.','(b) The vertical difference is 3−1 = 2.','The horizontal difference is −1−3 = −4, so m = 2/(−4) = −1/2.','Reversing both endpoint orders negates numerator and denominator together, leaving each slope unchanged.','Thus (a) rises from left to right and (b) falls from left to right.'],'answer':'(a) 1; (b) −1/2.','progressiveSolution':True,'solutionOrigin':'SpaceBook learning enhancement','sourceReferences':[{'page':184,'jpg':'080_page_2.jpg','verification':'Full source question and working visually checked'}]}]
